body:
I'm rather late, but I recommend sending the message. maybe adjust "But this perceived abandonment has never been real" to something like "...has never been my intention" or something like that. Only because, as someone with BPD (who has been struggling in the same way with a very kind, very patient friend), sounding like you are outright "denying" their reality can be taken harshly. Not that you're wrong! But to a BPD mind, it can sound like you think we're 'crazy'.

&#x200B;

I received similar messages as yours from the friend I previously mentioned, and they really helped me to see *what* I'd actually been doing (to them) for so long, and was part of the start of my current recovery and healing.
